From: naelolaiz <1333555+naelolaiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:30:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] main/cmake: no sphinx man pages when bootstrapping

With BOOTSTRAP or APORTS_BOOTSTRAP set, build cmake without
--sphinx-man and without py3-sphinx, which pulls in about 30 Python
modules. cmake itself, its bundled curl and nghttp2 and cmake-doc
(copyright and readme files) build as before.

Many packages build with cmake (brotli and c-ares for curl, tcpdump),
so on a new architecture this one edit takes about 33 source packages
off their way.

Without the variables the APKBUILD builds exactly what it built before.
Generic, not specific to riscv32.
---
 main/cmake/APKBUILD | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main/cmake/APKBUILD b/main/cmake/APKBUILD
index 6d33f64f328..be1ff82f475 100644
--- a/main/cmake/APKBUILD
+++ b/main/cmake/APKBUILD
@@ -16,12 +16,16 @@ makedepends="
 	libuv-dev
 	linux-headers
 	ncurses-dev
-	py3-sphinx
 	rhash-dev
 	samurai
 	xz-dev
 	zlib-dev
 	"
+if [ -z "$BOOTSTRAP" ] && [ -z "$APORTS_BOOTSTRAP" ]; then
+	# man pages; sphinx pulls in about 30 Python modules
+	makedepends="$makedepends py3-sphinx"
+	_sphinx_man="--sphinx-man"
+fi
 checkdepends="file"
 subpackages="
 	ccmake
@@ -48,7 +52,7 @@ build() {
 		--mandir=/share/man \
 		--datadir=/share/$pkgname \
 		--docdir=/share/doc/$pkgname \
-		--sphinx-man \
+		$_sphinx_man \
 		--no-system-cppdap \
 		--no-system-curl \
 		--no-system-jsoncpp \
-- 
